v. 7. devote (oneself) fully to; "He immersed himself into his studies"
v. 8. assimilate or take in; "The immigrants were quickly absorbed into society"
v. 9. consume all of one's attention or time; "Her interest in butterflies absorbs her completely"adj. 1. giving or marked by complete attention to; "that engrossed look or rapt delight"; "then wrapped in dreams"; "so intent on this fantastic...narrative that she hardly stirred"- Walter de la Mare; "rapt with wonder"; "wrapped in thought"
adj. 2. retained without reflection; "the absorbed light intensity"adj. 1. capable of arousing and holding the attention; "a fascinating story"n. 1. a concept or idea not associated with any specific instance; "he loved her only in the abstract--not in person"
