v. 3. give an affirmative reply to; respond favorably to; "I cannot accept your invitation"; "I go for this resolution"
v. 4. react favorably to; consider right and proper; "People did not accept atonal music at that time"; "We accept the idea of universal health care"
v. 5. admit into a group or community; "accept students for graduate study"; "We'll have to vote on whether or not to admit a new member"
