adj. 13. exhibiting or calling for sportsmanship or fair play; "a clean fight"; "a sporting solution of the disagreement"; "sportsmanlike conduct"
adj. 14. without difficulties or problems; "a clean test flight"
adj. 15. thorough and without qualification; "a clean getaway"; "a clean sweep"; "a clean break"
adj. 16. not carrying concealed weapons
adj. 17. free from clumsiness; precisely or deftly executed; "he landed a clean left on his opponent's cheek"; "a clean throw"; "the neat exactness of the surgeon's knife"
adj. 18. free of drugs; "after a long dependency on heroin she has been clean for 4 years"
