adj. 1. direct in spatial dimensions; proceeding without deviation or interruption; straight and short; "a direct route"; "a direct flight"; "a direct hit"
adj. 2. having no intervening persons, agents, conditions; "in direct sunlight"; "in direct contact with the voters"; "direct exposure to the disease"; "a direct link"; "the direct cause of the accident"; "direct vote"
adj. 3. straightforward in means or manner or behavior or language or action; "a direct question"; "a direct response"; "a direct approach"
