adj. 19. large and powerful; especially designed for heavy loads or rough work; "a heavy truck"; "heavy machinery"
adj. 20. dense or inadequately leavened and hence likely to cause distress in the alimentary canal; "a heavy pudding"
adj. 21. sharply inclined; "a heavy grade"
adj. 22. full of; bearing great weight; "trees heavy with fruit"; "vines weighed down with grapes"
adj. 23. requiring or showing effort; "heavy breathing"; "the subject made for labored reading"
