v. 28. discharge or direct or be discharged or directed as if in a continuous stream; "play water from a hose"; "The fountains played all day"
v. 29. make bets; "Play the races"; "play the casinos in Trouville"
v. 30. stake on the outcome of an issue; "I bet $100 on that new horse"; "She played all her money on the dark horse"
v. 31. shoot or hit in a particular manner; "She played a good backhand last night"
v. 32. use or move; "I had to play my queen"
v. 33. employ in a game or in a specific position; "They played him on first base"
v. 34. contend against an opponent in a sport, game, or battle; "Princeton plays Yale this weekend"; "Charlie likes to play Mary"
