adj. 3. in a state of extreme emotion; "wild with anger"; "wild with grief"
adj. 4. deviating widely from an intended course; "a wild bullet"; "he threw a wild pitch"
adj. 5. (of colors or sounds) intensely vivid or loud; "a violent clash of colors"; "her dress was a violent red"; "a violent noise"; "wild colors"; "wild shouts"
adj. 6. without a basis in reason or fact; "baseless gossip"; "the allegations proved groundless"; "idle fears"; "unfounded suspicions"; "unwarranted jealousy"
adj. 7. talking or behaving irrationally; "a raving lunatic"
adj. 8. involving risk or danger; "skydiving is a hazardous sport"; "extremely risky going out in the tide and fog"; "a wild financial scheme"
adj. 9. fanciful and unrealistic; foolish; "a fantastic idea of his own importance"
adj. 10. located in a dismal or remote area; desolate; "a desert island"; "a godforsaken wilderness crossroads"; "a wild stretch of land"; "waste places"
